# dumps.local.example — copy to `dumps.local` (git-ignored) and edit for YOUR machine.
#
# Each machine's dumps are often named differently from the shared catalog. This file remaps a
# database id (the modl, field 4 of the catalog) to the actual filename, or a glob, on THIS box,
# so make_manifest.sh finds them without editing the shared catalog.
#
# Format, one per line:   <modl> = <filename-or-glob>
#   - matched case-insensitively against catalog field 4
#   - value may be an exact filename or a glob; a glob must match exactly one file on disk
#   - paths are relative to the repo root
#
# Examples:
# customer-a = app-dump-postgres-2025-08-18.sql
# customer-b = *customer-b*dump*.sql
